{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500605-shifting-sands-real-time-travel-or-just-spell-duration-in-the-past","id":1500605,"title":"Shifting Sands: real time travel or just spell duration in the past?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-18T06:41:08-08:00","id":1500605,"title":"Shifting Sands: real time travel or just spell duration in the past?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <b>Shifting Sands: do you spend the spell duration in the past and that's it? Or do you time travel and start anew?</b><br /> <br /> I asked the same question on the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500526#post1500526\"><b>Ask a simple question, Awakened edition thread</b></a> (now closed). I got two answers from different posters:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> offered:<br /> &quot;<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500542#post1500542\">For <u>Shifting Sands</u>, you start the scene over. Anyone looking at them under Time Mage Sight will see the temporal distortion until you catch up to where you were when you cast the spell, but the effect is otherwise Lasting (I think).\u200b</a>&quot;</li> <li><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a> said:<br /> &quot;<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500548#post1500548\">For shifting sands, you'd go back X scenes for the duration of the shifting sands spell (which if it was longer than X scenes would mean you'd catch up to the present.) Any changes become lasting when you return to the present.</a>&quot;</li> </ol><br /> As that thread is closed, what is the real answer? Do you time travel and start from there anew OR do you spend the spell Duration in the past and catch up to the present with the changes?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T09:17:53-08:00","id":1500612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500605-shifting-sands-real-time-travel-or-just-spell-duration-in-the-past#post1500605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> <b>Shifting Sands: do you spend the spell duration in the past and that's it? Or do you time travel and start anew?</b><br /> <br /> I asked the same question on the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500526#post1500526\"><b>Ask a simple question, Awakened edition thread</b></a> (now closed). I got two answers from different posters:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> offered:<br /> &quot;<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500542#post1500542\">For <u>Shifting Sands</u>, you start the scene over. Anyone looking at them under Time Mage Sight will see the temporal distortion until you catch up to where you were when you cast the spell, but the effect is otherwise Lasting (I think).\u200b</a>&quot;</li> <li><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a> said:<br /> &quot;<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500548#post1500548\">For shifting sands, you'd go back X scenes for the duration of the shifting sands spell (which if it was longer than X scenes would mean you'd catch up to the present.) Any changes become lasting when you return to the present.</a>&quot;</li> </ol><br /> As that thread is closed, what is the real answer? Do you time travel and start from there anew OR do you spend the spell Duration in the past and catch up to the present with the changes?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Both answers are correct, You go back one scene, starting there, and then stay for the duration of the spell. When you catch up with the present either from the spell's duration ending or you spend the scene there and catch up to the present the changes you have made become lasting.<br /> <br /> If you cast spent 1 reach and cast the spell with a duration of 3 turns then you would travel back one scene and stay for 3 turns, then return to the present. Anything you changed in those 3 turns would become lasting, however since you went back 1 hour but only stayed 3 turns, you'd have no idea what happened in the remaining 59 mins after your 3 turns happened. If you increased the duration of the spell to a scene then you'd go back one scene and stay for the entire scene and therefore know what happens when you make changes. If you go back 2 scenes but only have a duration of one scene, then you'd have no idea what happens between the scene you stay for and the scene after you leave...<br /> <br /> A potency 3 shifting sands spell with a duration of 1 turn would mean you go back 3 turns, spend 1 turn to make changes then return to the present. Skipping 2 turns.<br /> <br /> While in the past you show up as a temporal anomaly to time sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-18-2023, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T14:20:51-08:00","id":1500659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Mage: The Awakening 2ed, page 123</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Weaving spells can alter nearly any property of a target without transforming it into something completely different. Solid steel can be transmuted to liquid (Matter), a sword can be enchanted to damage beings in Twilight (Death or Spirit), <b>or a few seconds of time can be rewritten (Time)</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Shifting Sands</i> sends a mage to the past, substituting their present self for their past self, they re-live [Potency] turns and then the spell ends, the changes become Lasting and the present changes to adjust for them. Its more of a scalpel as compared to <i>Corridors of Time</i>, and it makes it harder to go back multiple scenes. But a deliberate mage can leverage it to make a big difference.<br /> <br /> While in the past, the moment of substitution triggers Peripheral Mage Sight. The subject and anything they interact with registered under Time Sight. Should the Imago be dispelled before the full duration, the subject is catapulted back to the present and no changes take place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-18-2023, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T03:59:44-08:00","id":1500716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500605-shifting-sands-real-time-travel-or-just-spell-duration-in-the-past?p=1500659#post1500659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Shifting Sands</i> sends a mage to the past, substituting their present self for their past self, they re-live [Potency] turns and then the spell ends, the changes become Lasting and the present changes to adjust for them. Its more of a scalpel as compared to <i>Corridors of Time</i>, and it makes it harder to go back multiple scenes. But a deliberate mage can leverage it to make a big difference.<br /> <br /> While in the past, the moment of substitution triggers Peripheral Mage Sight. The subject and anything they interact with registered under Time Sight. Should the Imago be dispelled before the full duration, the subject is catapulted back to the present and no changes take place.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way the spell is written(if read in isolation) it does seem to assume you go back potency turns and then return to the present. No duration required.<br /> <br /> And paying for the duration twice seems unlike most other spells (like you pay -6 to go back three turns, and then need another -6 to add duration to the spell so it lasts...)<br /> <br /> But that doesn't allow for things like the spell being dispelled while you are in the past (rules on pg 186). And the way corridors of time works it explicitly uses potency (primary) to overcome the withstand (from Temporal sympathy) and duration to determine how long you remain in the past.<br /> <br /> Making Shifting Sands work more like Corridors seems to be the preferred interpretation on the forums, and one which i have come to agree with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T04:11:02-08:00","id":1500718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500605-shifting-sands-real-time-travel-or-just-spell-duration-in-the-past?p=1500659#post1500659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Shifting Sands</i> sends a mage to the past, substituting their present self for their past self, they re-live [Potency] turns and then the spell ends, the changes become Lasting and the present changes to adjust for them. Its more of a scalpel as compared to <i>Corridors of Time</i>, and it makes it harder to go back multiple scenes. But a deliberate mage can leverage it to make a big difference.<br /> <br /> While in the past, the moment of substitution triggers Peripheral Mage Sight. The subject and anything they interact with registered under Time Sight. Should the Imago be dispelled before the full duration, the subject is catapulted back to the present and no changes take place.</div> </div> </div> </div>They go back in time potency turns (or scenes with reach) and relive the spell's Duration...potency for determining how far back, the duration for how long they stay. Sometimes duration will be longer than potency in which case they catch up with the present.<br /> <br /> Potency 10 with a duration of 1 turn would be going back 10 turns and redoing the first turn then traveling back skipping turns 2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9 and 10. Potency 10 with a duration of 5 turns would be going back 10 turns and redoing turns 1,2,3,4,5 then returning to the present skipping over turns 6,7,8,9 and 10.<br /> <br /> Potency 5 with a duration of a scene would be going back 5 turns and redoing all 5 turns with the spell ending after the 5th turn even though it was a scene because you caught up with the present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-19-2023, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}